  <details class="audit-details audit-methodology"><summary>How the scoring works and what it can’t tell you</summary><div>
    <p>This is an independent directional self-assessment. It doesn’t inspect bills, verify your answers, calculate savings, or certify a FinOps practice. The scores, four areas, pattern names, and cutoffs are Cloud &amp; Capital’s own rubric. They have not been calibrated against an industry dataset.</p>
    <p>Each scored answer is worth 0–3 points. Each area needs at least two of its three questions scored. We divide the points by the maximum for those scored answers, multiply by 100, and round to a whole number. Unknown and not applicable answers are excluded, not scored as zero. They remain visible in the answer count.</p>
    <p>Understand the spending averages the rounded scores for Understand the bill and Connect cost to value. Use it in decisions averages Check before committing and Follow through. We round each average. Both axes need valid scores in their two areas, requiring at least eight scored answers overall. The map divides at 67 points on each axis, matching the pattern labels.</p>
    <p>When there is a known gap, the first step uses the lowest scored question within the lowest scoring area that contains a 0 or 1 answer. An area where all scored answers are 2 or 3 does not trigger a repair suggestion. For a tied area score, we first consider the lowest individual answer, then use this order: Check before committing, Follow through, Understand the bill, Connect cost to value. Tied questions use their questionnaire order. This is a starting point to check, not proof of the most important business problem.</p>
    <p>If there aren’t enough scored answers, start by checking the missing information or whether the scope fits. If every scored answer describes a working or consistent practice, we suggest maintaining it; unknown answers still need checking. Keep scope, participants, and exclusions consistent before comparing two assessments. Changing a scope clears the previous answers.</p>
    <p>Concepts adapted independently from the FinOps Foundation’s <a href="https://www.finops.org/framework/">FinOps Framework</a>, <a href="https://www.finops.org/framework/maturity-model/">Maturity Model</a>, and <a href="https://www.finops.org/wg/finops-assessment/">Assessment Guide</a>, under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. The Foundation does not endorse this tool. Our scoring is separate from its assessment, and the most advanced practice is not always the right goal.</p>
    <p>Rubric reviewed October 23, 2026. The questionnaire runs in this tab without sending answers to an AI provider or saving them for another visit. Basic site analytics record tool activity without the questionnaire’s answers or scores.</p>
  </div></details>
